# results/ is ignored by default: it accumulates exploratory runs, superseded
# protocols and LLM response caches. The four artefacts below are the exception
# -- they are the ones the paper reports (Table 2, the significance tests and
# Fig. 1), and shipping them lets `python src/plots.py` and
# `python experiments/run_significance.py` run on a clean clone without first
# repeating ~2.5 h of CPU.
results/*
results/.llm_cache*
!results/tcga_brca_cv20x5.json
!results/tcga_brca_cv20x5_k60.json
!results/tcga_brca_cv20x5_k80.json
!results/significance_20x5.json

